  "text": "This series argues the decisions behind the answers: why a model fails on new data, which loss fits a problem, what serving costs, and how you'd know it broke. The track's pages ask a hundred and sixty-seven questions. This video answers one. Ten more answer the rest, each once, and a question two pages share is answered once for both. First generalization, then the models and how they learn, coding, statistics, deep learning, and NLP. Then system design, and shipping and monitoring models. Last, the two LLM parts: serving them, and evaluating them. Every topic page has concept checks, five challenges run in the browser, and a hundred and ten multiple-choice questions cover the whole track. So the first thing an ML round still tests is whether a model works on data it hasn't seen. Next: generalization and evaluation.",
